From 5692a579175598a588849058d364f47fc3bd4934 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:17:00 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add GSWIP-3.0 PCE table engine and parser
 microcode

Add the PCE (Packet Classification Engine) indirect-table access
engine and the parser microcode load for the GSWIP-3.0 switch cores:

 - gsw_flow_pce.c: the four indirect-table helpers
   (gsw_pce_table_read/write and the key-search variants) driving
   the PCE_TBL_* register window with busy-poll timeouts, the
   GSWIP-3.0 table-shape descriptor and register-offset arrays, and
   gsw_pmicro_code_init(), which loads the 256-row parser microcode
   at probe time in the hardware-required order: disable per-port
   FDMA/SDMA, arm the switch arbiter (GCTRL.SE=1) BEFORE clearing
   MC_VALID, load the 256 rows, set MC_VALID, enable the BM RMON
   counters, and select the GSWIP-3.0 GL_MOD queue mode. Reversing
   the arbiter/MC_VALID order leaves the FDMA arbiter unarmed - a
   regression documented from the earlier v5.10 port.

 - pce_microcode_table.h: the 256-entry parser microcode array,
   reproduced verbatim from the vendor source.

Derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198),
switch-api module (gsw_tbl_rw.c, gsw_flow_core.c, gsw_flow_pce.c) -
Copyright (c) 2012-2015 Lantiq Deutschland GmbH, (c) 2016-2017
Intel Corporation; notices added to both files. GSWIP-2.2/3.1
branches are not ported; error returns are strengthened so a failed
row write aborts the load instead of leaving MC_VALID asserted over
partial microcode.

The per-port enable tail (FDMA/SDMA re-enable, PMAC tables,
special-tag ingress) follows in the next patch.

